---
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
---
<div class="ridge-panel ridge-subscribe" style="--ridge-index:1">
<article class="journey-bento page-frame" aria-labelledby="journey-subscribe-title">
 <div class="jb-composition">
  <header class="jb-heading"><div class="jb-identity"><span>02 / SUBSCRIBE A CAR</span><span>Car subscription · Mobile app</span></div><h3 id="journey-subscribe-title">From browsing <em>to booking.</em></h3></header>
  <figure class="jb-showcase jb-phones">
   <div class="jb-phone-sequence">
    <img src="/review-images/subscribe-browse-360.webp" width="360" height="1318" alt="Subscribe Me vehicle browsing interface with car availability and monthly pricing." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    <img src="/review-images/subscribe-detail-480.webp" width="1440" height="2300" alt="Subscribe Me vehicle details and booking interface." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
   </div>
   <figcaption>Subscribe Me · Original mobile interface designs</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="jb-story"><p>Joining at Sprint 4 to deliver production UI and extend the existing design system for Subscribe Me, a car subscription product.</p>
   <dl class="jb-facts"><div><dt>Contribution</dt><dd>UI Designer — Delivery Phase</dd></div><div><dt>Client &amp; delivery team</dt><dd>AW Rostamani · RBB Global</dd></div><div><dt>Design scope</dt><dd>Booking flows, checkout and design system components</dd></div></dl>
   <a class="text-link" href="/case-studies/subscribe-me-case-study.html">Read Full Case Study <Arrow /></a>
  </div>
 </div>
</article>
</div>
<div class="ridge-panel ridge-utworx" style="--ridge-index:2">
<article class="journey-bento page-frame" aria-labelledby="journey-utworx-title">
 <div class="jb-composition">
  <header class="jb-heading"><div class="jb-identity"><span>03 / UTWorX</span><span>Enterprise · Asset management</span></div><h3 id="journey-utworx-title">Clarity under <em>complexity.</em></h3></header>
  <figure class="jb-showcase jb-dashboard"><picture>
   <source media="(max-width:650px)" srcset="/review-images/utworx-focus-480.webp 480w, /review-images/utworx-focus-800.webp 800w" sizes="calc(100vw - 80px)" width="1700" height="1600" />
   <img src="/review-images/utworx-overview-1280.webp" srcset="/review-images/utworx-overview-800.webp 800w, /review-images/utworx-overview-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width:800px) 90vw, 45vw" width="4320" height="4008" alt="UTWorX enterprise dashboard showing work summary and asset overview." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
  </picture><figcaption>Original asset and maintenance management interface</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="jb-story"><p>Make the platform easier to use without changing what it does. A redesign for three operational roles, each with different information needs and time pressures.</p>
   <dl class="jb-scope" aria-label="Delivery scope, not usability outcomes"><div><dt>Screens</dt><dd>16</dd></div><div><dt>User roles</dt><dd>3</dd></div><div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>2 weeks</dd></div><div><dt>Functionality changes</dt><dd>Zero</dd></div></dl>
   <p class="jb-note">Lead UI/UX Designer · Formal usability metrics were not collected within the two-week scope.</p>
   <a class="text-link" href="/case-studies/utworx-case-study.html">Read Full Case Study <Arrow /></a>
  </div>
 </div>
</article>
</div>
